<title>HUNGARY: Riziko, Deviza open mixed.</title>
<headline>Riziko, Deviza open mixed.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary's two new stocks, Riziko Factory and Masodik Deviza Factory, started trading mixed but in low volumes, traders said.</p>
<p>Currency futures trading firm Masodik Deviza Factory opened at 13,550 forints, while venture capital company Riziko Factory at 9,500 forints. Both were issued at 10,000 forints.</p>
<p>Traders said activity in the two, one deal in each until 1040 GMT, showed the place they will play in the bourse.</p>
<p>&quot;The activity reflected the papers will not play a leading role on the bourse,&quot; one trader said. &quot;Investors will not kill each other to buy these stocks.&quot;</p>
<p>Both stocks were introduced to the listed &quot;B&quot; category.</p>
<p>-- Emese Bartha, Budapest newsroom +36 1 327-4040</p>
</text>
